    "body": "**The D1 result: the main-line core keeps its quaternion transport.** References #820 and #973. D1 was pre-registered in the whole-project synthesis §4 and assigned to the cloud track. Work card, with the outcome: [#973 comment](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/issues/973#issuecomment-5864504193).\n\n## Result\n\n*Measured.* Development NLL on the 512 evenly spaced windows (131,072 targets):\n\n| Seed | Quaternion transport | Identity transport | Identity − quaternion |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 2.599845 | 2.670985 | **+0.0711** |\n| 2 | 2.580265 | 2.657687 | **+0.0774** |\n\n- **Reading.** The rule, fixed before any run: keep the transport only if it wins by at least 0.02 nats in both seeds. It does in both, so it is **kept**.\n  - It led at every 64-window evaluation, and its lead grew to about 0.06–0.09 by 1,000 updates.\n- **Design.** The arms differ only in `rotation`: both are pinned at MLP 749 with `stack_mlp=` (#1437). That removes cycle 4's `norot` confound, where a wider MLP absorbed the rotation's parameters and measured only +0.059 over one seed.\n  - The identity arm has 332,928 fewer parameters, which the pre-registered design accepts.\n- **Cost of the transport.** It carries 332,928 parameters and cost 8–10% of training throughput here. Its D11 export needs table-served quaternion products.\n- **Scope.** Code data, 1,000 updates, two seeds and one host. This PR does not show:\n  - an effect at full exposure, on prose or dialogue, or at 10–30M parameters;\n  - which property does the work (a parameter-matched real-gate control would separate \"extra gate rows\").\n- **Derived** (in the note): the transport composes token-dependent rotations along the prefix, `h_t = U_t Σ_s Λ U_s⁻¹ b_s`. Its frames depend on the whole prefix, so ruling 11's endpoint factoring does not apply.\n\n## What is added\n\n- `docs/integration/transport-attribution-d1-2026-09-28.md`: the note, covering design, results, curves, reading, serving consequences and costs.\n- `docs/evidence/transport-attribution-d1-2026-09-28/`: the packet. It holds:\n  - four sealed report roots' records: claim, report, seal manifest, model configuration;\n  - training logs, the runner and the chain log;\n  - `packet.json`, with the computed decision and the SHA-256 of every file.\n- `docs/integration/current-state.md`: a D1 entry under the lab track's geometric-stack item.\n\n## Checks\n\n- All four roots were claimed, sealed and verified by the executable. Every model's SHA-256 equals its report's `model_sha256`.\n- The packet's 23 listed files match `packet.json`, and the note's relative links resolve.\n- `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py` passes.\n- The PR changes documentation and evidence only.\n\n**Cost** (*Measured*):\n- 3 h 21 min of wall time for the four arms (06:14–09:36 UTC), two threads per arm, plus about 20 minutes of build and smoke run.\n- 107 MB of retained models in the lab sandbox, pinned by SHA-256.\n- No external compute.\n\nThis branch was cut fresh from `main` (`e8cd2c5b`) because #1437 squash-merged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018jzJYgXbX8FmctqekthjLJ\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_018jzJYgXbX8FmctqekthjLJ)_",
