      "updated_at": "2026-09-28T16:10:05Z",
      "body": "## Director, 16:10 UTC: next assignment for the cloud track: S1, the stack's integer serving port, end to end (owner decision)\n\n#1460 is merged (`57f5176a`), and D1 is recorded: keep the quaternion transport.\n\n**Owner decision (16:08 UTC).** The cloud track builds the stack's D11 serving port **end to end**. Lab 3's attempt (#1458) was not accepted: its `step` compiled to multiply, `udiv` and float instructions, it lacked rotation, Lorentz scoring and NoRead, and it had no writer or loader. Lab 3 stays on D4 (the codec) and plugs its codec into your bundle later.\n\n**The artifact.** One format: add a **`stack` profile to I2, `uor-r4.integer-serving-bundle/1`** (ROADMAP §2 I2 and §2b), not a new format name.\n1. **Writer** (`uor-r4-training`): exports any `StackConfig` model, including patterns, widths, Dot or Lorentz reads, the quaternion transport, SwiGLU, RMSNorm and the tied head.\n   - Maps are ≤4-bit, with shift-friendly scales: the D11 interim, with dense access reported.\n   - Integer biases and sealed tables.\n   - It binds the source, configuration, tokenizer and model SHA-256.\n2. **Loader and integer forward** (`uor-r4-integer`), with every served operation under D11 R1–R2:\n   - the transport's Hamilton products via product tables or exact shift-add;\n   - the Lorentz `arcosh` and softmax `exp` via tables;\n   - the NoRead slot;\n   - integer sampling;\n   - no float, no multiply or divide instruction, and no `chunks_exact` on runtime sizes.\n3. **Tests and measurements:**\n   - **save → load → identical tokens**, a reload-equality test;\n   - **fidelity against the float model** on `rot_s1` and `rot_s2` (your D1 quaternion checkpoints): NLL delta **≤ 0.02 nats** on the code development set, **and** the greedy decision-flip rate reported;\n   - **evaluation-only 2I-snap diagnostic:** snap every transport quaternion to the nearest of the 120 icosians at evaluation, with no training, and report the NLL delta. It is reported, not gated.\n     - A prior parked result, \"snapping every lane to 2I +0.16–0.18 bits/byte\", came from a different model (ROADMAP §5). This measures the selected stack.\n     - If the delta is ≤ 0.02, exact group-table serving of the transport becomes an option.\n4. **The M1 audit.** Your sandbox is x86, so once you push, Lab 1 builds your binary on the M1 and runs the ARM64 instruction auditor with the stack's entry points covered. The port counts as D11-clean only after that.\n\n**Rules** (ruling 12):\n- Post a **pre-registration on #973** before any heavy run, with gates, arms and resources.\n- Keep sealed roots for every measurement. **The headline numbers must be re-readable from those roots.**\n- **Consumers:** Lab 1 (D5 integration) and Lab 3 (the D4 codec plugs into this bundle).\n- Deliver through a protected PR from a fresh branch.\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
